{"id": "EUVD-2026-92119", "enisaUuid": "a7abf84c-8197-3b2b-b2f9-50c85bad1d0a", "description": "go-micro before 6.0.0 contains an improper certificate validation vulnerability that allows network attackers to impersonate services because the shared TLS helper sets InsecureSkipVerify to true by default. Man-in-the-middle attackers can present any certificate to intercept or modify gRPC transport, HTTP and RabbitMQ broker, and Consul or etcd registry traffic, including authentication tokens and credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-04T17:09:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-05T20:28:54", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/micro/go-micro/issues/2963", "https://github.com/micro/go-micro/commit/c7657f73f45cf839e643db10f28703eeab7299c3", "https://github.com/micro/go-micro/blob/v5.30.0/internal/util/tls/tls.go#L43-L67", "https://github.com/micro/go-micro", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/go-micro-before-6.0.0-disabled-tls-certificate-verification-via-tls-config-helper"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-105216", "GHSA-p6q5-cmw8-pqqg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2f90567f-e3a1-3ecc-9160-f0aeb24ec547", "product": {"name": "go-micro", "vendor": {"name": "micro"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2fa0fe12-c5df-3c03-9def-7aed804601f5", "vendor": {"name": "micro"}}], "isExploited": false}